The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (S.len > 1) {
    if      (dir == LEFT  && S.dir == RIGHT)
        S.dir = RIGHT;
    else if (dir == RIGHT && S.dir == LEFT)
        S.dir = LEFT;
    else if (dir == UP    && S.dir == DOWN)
        S.dir = DOWN;
    else if (dir == DOWN  && S.dir == UP)
        S.dir = UP;
}
```
Reason:
The condition `if (S.len > 1)` restricts the snake from changing direction when its length is greater than 1, which is problematic because it prevents valid direction changes that do not result in self-collision, leading to unintended behavior in the game.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
else
    S.dir = dir;
```
Reason:
The addition of `else S.dir = dir;` allows the snake to change its direction to the new input direction when it is valid, regardless of its length, thus enabling proper navigation and adherence to the game's mechanics.

